            <ArticleTitle>Adverse reactions to 1975 bivalent influenza vaccine in children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>271-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A questionnaire survey was undertaken to investigate incidence and types of reactions to a bivalent, zonally purified, killed influenza vaccine administered to 155 children aged 1 to 18 years in 1975. Local or systemic reactions or both occurred in 42 children (27%). However, these reactions were not considered serious and should not constitute a major drawback to future influenza programs in children under 3 years of age.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
